WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:03.211
Kurt Russell:
From the time I was a kid,...

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:04.879
(Ground cracking)

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:07.590
...there are certain characters,
certain things that you've seen...

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.466
♪♪

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:10.301
...that have an impact on you, that stay with you.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:11.594
 (Eerie sound)

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:13.430
(Screaming)
(Destruction SFX)

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:15.557
And Godzilla is one of them.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.518
(Roaring)

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.733
It's an honor to be invited by

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.278
our friends and collaborators at Toho and at Legendary

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.405
Chris Black:
to play in this monster universe.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:35.994
Chris Black:
There is a legacy that goes back 70 years 
that we want to be respectful of.

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:40.457
 So we have to honor everything and maintain consistency.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:44.335
Matt Fraction:
And the thing that was exciting was to tell a human-scaled story

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:46.546
on a monster-scaled stage.

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:48.131
Chambers deep in the bedrock.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.382
Lee Shaw:
There's something down there.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.343
Lee Shaw:
Oh my god, go, go, go!

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.680
The movies are so grand and epic.

00:00:55.972 --> 00:01:00.059
Anna Sawai:
And with a show like this, we get the luxury to explore it in 10 episodes,

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.520
Anna Sawai:
which means more detail, more drama.

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:04.147
It's really exciting.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.190
 Hit the gas, Doc.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:07.358
(Engine Revving)

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:10.153
There's two timelines happening in this show,

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:13.072
Anders Holm:
one in the 50s and one in the modern era.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:17.243
Anders Holm:
And the present-day characters discovered that they're part of this interconnected legacy.

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:18.995
Did our dad really work for Monarch?

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:20.622
It is your family business.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.873
It's the family curse.

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:25.251
My son, Wyatt, and I, we're playing the same person.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.798
We go from his period of time back in the 50s to modern day.

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:32.842
We had been asked to be in the same movie, 
usually as father and son,

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:37.514
but the idea of playing the same person had an artistic element to it that drew us to it.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:39.307
The things I do for Monarch.

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:40.892
Wouldn't have made it this far without you.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:44.646
Every time I think we're searching for dad, turns out there's some Monarch business in the way.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.065
I'm sorry everything is tangled up together.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.359
Lee Shaw:
But yes, all these roads lead to one place.

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:51.361
This crew that we follow in the present day

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:53.988
are just as new to the world as a new viewer might be.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:54.948
Welcome to Monarch.

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:56.699
Sorry.

00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:59.118
They're not scientists and superheroes.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.995
Matt Fraction:
They are regular people.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:02.664
Matt Fraction:
Everything is new and insane.

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.376
Every time you go to locations in the show,

00:02:06.876 --> 00:02:08.711
Mari Yamamoto:
it's a completely different world.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.255
We shot one at Glacier.

00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:10.880
Move!

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.507
(Beast roaring)

00:02:12.507 --> 00:02:13.716
We shot in the desert.

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:15.677
We went to Tokyo.

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.137
Just amazing.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.305
(Rocks crumbling)

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:24.435
It's the most rewarding experience to be 
part of something this cool, this big.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:25.311
Lee Shaw:
Go. Go. Go.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:30.275
I feel like the show we all set out to do was 
going to be epic and adventurous.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:32.569
But all of the underlying feelings are there too.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:33.987
This changes everything.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:36.364
Lee Shaw:
No, oh my God!

00:02:36.364 --> 00:02:38.074
(Intense music)

00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:43.037
The audience who loves the Monsterverse will see a world they recognize and feel it's been honored.

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:48.001
The new fans will watch this and go, wow, 
this is the story that I'm being drawn into.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.169
This is a height of entertainment.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.963
Wyatt Russell:
It has action and excitement.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.965
And all these monsters are pretty gnarly.

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.174
(chuckles)
I'll say that.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.050
(Water cascading)

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.721
(Roaring)

